# Language Conventions

> **Rule**: Code in ENGLISH, User Interface in SPANISH (LATAM target audience)

## Two-Layer Language Strategy

| Layer | Language | Examples |
|-------|----------|----------|
| **Code** | English | Variables, functions, comments, files, JSDoc |
| **UI** | Spanish | Labels, buttons, messages, placeholders, titles |

---

## CODE LAYER (English)

### Variables and Functions

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: English code
const appointmentDate = new Date();
const isAvailable = checkAvailability(slot);
function handleBookingSubmit() {}
function validateAppointment() {}

// ❌ BAD: Spanish code
const fechaCita = new Date();
function manejarEnvioReserva() {}
```

### Comments and Documentation

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: English comments
// Check if the slot is available before booking

/**
 * Fetches available time slots for a professional
 * @param professionalId - The professional's unique identifier
 */
function getAvailableSlots(professionalId: string) {}

// ❌ BAD: Spanish comments
// Verificar si el slot está disponible
```

### File and Folder Names

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
features/appointments/
components/BookingCard.tsx
hooks/useAvailability.ts

// ❌ BAD
features/citas/
components/TarjetaReserva.tsx
```

### Console and Error Logs

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: Internal errors in English
throw new Error('Invalid appointment date');
console.error('Failed to fetch professionals');
```

### Git Commits

```bash
# ✅ GOOD
git commit -m "feat: add appointment booking flow"

# ❌ BAD
git commit -m "feat: agregar flujo de reserva de citas"
```

